1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,119
Number two this is a golden pillar for me it's a no phone rule.
第二个习惯，是我的一根黄金支柱：不使用手机的规则。

2
00:00:05,119 --> 00:00:11,040
So I have a rule where for the first let's say two hours of the day and the last hour of the day.
我的规则是，一天开始后的，比如说两个小时，以及结束前的最后一个小时，

3
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:17,040
I have my phone on do not disturb and I really try and not go on it unless it's for something I absolutely need to.
我会把手机设成勿扰模式，尽量不用，除非确实有必须做的事。

4
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:26,000
And the way I do this is I use on the iphone it's called the do not disturb feature which basically means you won't get any notifications po up on your phone.
具体做法是用 iPhone 上的“勿扰”功能，基本上就是不会有通知在手机上“po up”（字幕疑点）。

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,399
It doesn't put it on airplane mode or anything like that.
它不会让手机进入飞行模式之类的状态。

6
00:00:28,399 --> 00:00:32,200
So everything is still coming through they're just not popping up on your home phone.
所以信息仍然会进来，只是不在你的“home phone”上弹出（原字幕如此）。

7
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:35,800
Which means you're not being distracted first thing in the morning.
这意味着，你一大早就不会被分心。这对我非常重要。

8
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:43,720
This is very very important for me this is when I'm doing my movement so I'm waking up and I'm going straight to the gym or I'm going straight for my walk.
这时我在运动：起床后直接去健身房，或者直接出去散步。

9
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:46,080
It's something I like to do first thing in the morning.
这是我喜欢一大早就做的事。

10
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:53,160
If I had my phone not on do not disturb I'd be waking up to my alarm and instantly seeing all my notifications.
如果手机没有设成勿扰，我会伴着闹钟醒来，立刻看到所有通知。

11
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:57,679
And what that does is it puts me in an imed immediate space of distraction.
这就会让我立刻进入一种分心的状态（字幕保留了 imed 的起句）。

12
00:00:57,679 --> 00:01:02,600
So that means I'm not I don't have that space and time for myself right.
也就是说，我就没有留给自己的时间和空间了，对吧？

13
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:08,839
The phone is such a beautiful tool we've got we can access the world in our pockets.
手机是我们拥有的一个很美妙的工具，让我们能把世界装进口袋。

14
00:01:08,839 --> 00:01:11,959
But it also means our attention is grabbed constantly.
但这也意味着，我们的注意力不断被抓走。

15
00:01:11,959 --> 00:01:20,880
And so I find using this do not disturb feature or the no phone rule is a way for you to commit time for yourself and keep that sacred.
所以我发现，使用勿扰功能或不用手机的规则，是为自己投入时间，并珍视这段时间的一种方式。

16
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:27,240
And what I love doing is when I'm ready to be distracted that's when I take my phone off do not disturb in the morning.
我喜欢的是：等我准备好接受打扰时，早上才把手机的勿扰模式关掉。

17
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:35,279
And it's this really nice practice of I've just had 2 3 hours to myself and I'm now choosing that I'm prepared to be distracted.
这是个很好的做法：我刚刚独处了两三个小时，现在选择让自己准备好接受打扰。

18
00:01:35,279 --> 00:01:40,520
So this this really nice way of just controlling your energy and conserving it for yourself.
所以，这是一种很好的方式，让你掌控精力，把它留给自己。

19
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:49,720
And the other thing I'll say is especially with the night one think about the energy and pace of you scrolling on social media constantly right.
另外，尤其是睡前那一条，想想你不停刷社交媒体时那种精力状态和节奏。

20
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:56,630
It's like dopamine hit dopamine hit you're just distracted very very short grabby style energy right.
像是一次次多巴胺刺激，一直被分心，是那种很短促、抓人注意的状态。

21
00:01:56,640 --> 00:02:02,800
You're just like always needing something to top it up to top it up to top it up and it's very like quick frantic energy.
你好像一直需要东西把它补上、补上、再补上，那是一种很快、很躁动的状态。

22
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:15,320
If you can actually switch that off a decent amount of time before you go to bed that actually gets your energy back into this just slow not distracted kind of neutral state.
如果你能在睡前提前相当一段时间关掉它，精力就会回到慢下来、不分心、比较中性的状态。

23
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:21,239
If you have scrolled and then try and go to sleep it's highly likely that it takes you quite some time to go to sleep.
如果刷过手机再尝试睡觉，很可能要花相当一段时间才睡得着。

24
00:02:21,239 --> 00:02:26,109
And for me personally I can only put this down to the way that I get revved up.
对我个人而言，我只能把这归因于手机让我变得兴奋起来的方式。

25
00:02:26,119 --> 00:02:31,279
Just being on my phone especially the way we consume short form content and social media.
尤其是我们消费短内容和社交媒体的方式。

26
00:02:31,279 --> 00:02:39,080
So having that rule has been incredible for my sleep it's been incredible for my own connection with myself.
因此，这个规则对我的睡眠帮助很大，对我与自己的连接也很有帮助，

27
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:47,000
And just really protecting me from being distracted I mean we've got all day to be on our phone a lot of us use our phone for work.
也确实保护我不被分心。我的意思是，我们一整天都能用手机，很多人也用手机工作。

28
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,600
It's basically on my desk all day when I'm working so I'm never without it.
工作时它基本一整天都在我的桌上，所以我从来离不开它。

29
00:02:51,600 --> 00:03:00,119
So I can choose to just switch that off and use that do not disturb feature as kind of like a barrier for my own time.
所以我可以选择把它关掉，用勿扰功能作为保护自己时间的一道屏障。

30
00:03:00,119 --> 00:03:10,920
So this has been a habit that I have found incredibly profound to just create that time and space for myself and opt in and out of destruction.
所以，我发现这个习惯意义很深：为自己留出时间和空间，并选择进入或退出“destruction”（原字幕如此）。

31
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:16,200
And just as a quick aside like if you're someone who is trying to build a different life for yourself.
顺便说一句，如果你正在为自己打造不一样的生活，

32
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:22,080
If you're trying to focus if you're trying to be a little bit more organized or disciplined use this feature throughout the day as well.
如果你想专注一点，或更有条理、更自律一点，也可以全天使用这个功能。

33
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:28,959
You know if you've got an hour to do work it's really hard sometimes to have the phone face down because you're tempted to look at it.
你知道，如果有一小时的工作要做，有时把手机反扣着也很难，因为你会忍不住想看。

34
00:03:28,959 --> 00:03:32,799
And you know we check it we have those natural tendencies and urges.
我们会去看手机，我们有这些自然的倾向和冲动。

35
00:03:32,799 --> 00:03:39,480
But if you use a do not disturb feature it's still there you can see the time you're not distracted by that notification going off.
但如果用了勿扰功能，手机还在那里，你也能看时间，却不会被响起的通知打断。

36
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:47,720
So this has been an amazing feature I really love it and using it as the way I start and end my day has been really really powerful.
所以这个功能非常棒，我很喜欢；用它开始和结束一天，对我很有力量。
